Abdominal surgical robots are sophisticated systems designed for minimally invasive procedures within the abdominal cavity. These platforms provide surgeons with precise instrument control, high‑definition three‑dimensional visualization, and multi‑articulated “wristed” tools that replicate the dexterity of the human hand while operating through small trocar incisions. Typical configurations comprise a surgeon’s console, a patient‑side cart equipped with robotic arms, and high‑resolution endoscopic cameras that together enable procedures such as cholecystectomies, colorectal resections, hernia repairs, bariatric surgeries, and complex hepatobiliary operations.

