What are Abdominal Surgical Robots?
Abdominal surgical robots are computer‑assisted devices that augment a surgeon’s capabilities by translating hand movements at a console into highly precise motions of miniature instruments inside the patient’s abdomen. The technology combines real‑time imaging, ergonomic console design, and instrument articulation that exceeds the degrees of freedom achievable with conventional laparoscopic tools. By reducing tremor, enhancing depth perception, and enabling motion scaling, these systems strive to improve clinical outcomes, shorten operative times, and decrease postoperative pain and length of stay.

